From 20ef111cd41597ce7f0081d43e07ae88937c7574 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:48:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(text): place typed text in a TrueType outline font
 as closed shapes

Add camcraft_geometry::outline_text: a bounds-checked TrueType reader
(cmap 4/12, loca, glyf simple and composite, hmtx, OS/2 cap height),
quadratic contours flattened within 0.005 mm, and a sketch of closed
chains on the layer "text". Unreadable fonts, CFF outlines, font
collections, missing glyphs and crossing outlines are refused by name.

Add the undoable InsertOutlineText command and the MCP tool
insert_outline_text. The profile keeps the shapes, not the font, and
2D operations take it as their source like a DXF profile.

Fixes #3072

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
